    {
      "id": "cp_mrs_ctrl",
      "gender": "Female",
      "hasShell": false,
      "partNumber": "90980-10897",
      "description": "MR-S EHPS pump — control connector housing (pigtail 82998-12440). Toyota generic connector family (Sumitomo TS090 / Yazaki 090-II series) - NOT a TE Connectivity part (checked TE's site, no match; corrected from an earlier draft that mislabeled this as 90980-10942, which is actually the small ignition-enable connector). 6 physical cavities, only 2 used: pin 2 = speed-pulse output (SPD Out), pin 6 = relay-request output (grounds k_eps coil 85 when pump wants power). Confirmed directly from Daniel's photos of the pump (DIY Electric Car Forums 'MR2 Gen3 Power Steering Help' diagram, connector 'B') - both pin numbers are legible in the source image. Housing/pigtail part numbers sourced from a separate DIYElectricCar thread ('Power Steering using Toyota MR2 EHPS pump') - cross-check against the pump in hand before ordering. - OWNED (Daniel confirmed on hand)",
      "manufacturer": "Toyota",
      "configurations": [
        {
          "id": "cfg",
          "contactPartId": "ct_toy_ts"
        }
      ],
      "numberOfCavities": 6
    },
